I build the software that makes custom hardware usable: compilers, simulators, and embedded firmware — the core system layers that translate hardware constraints into reliable, high-performance platforms. That work often starts in co-design with hardware teams, because the decisions made there determine what the platform can become.

I specialize in the #strong["0 to 1" phase] of deep-tech systems, applying modern software engineering rigor to resource-constrained environments and platforms like RISC-V. By turning architectural constraints into opportunities, I help teams establish clarity and alignment from the ground up.

The results of this approach are concrete: I led a custom edge AI accelerator from architecture study through toolchain and runtime to RISC-V SoC integration, and I currently enable edge AI on space-grade compute with Frontgrade Gaisler.

This site is a space for me to share my work and ideas publicly. On my #link("/blog")[blog], I explore the intersection of technology and human systems — from technical deep-dives into embedded systems and toolchain development to broader reflections on engineering efficiency and leadership.

My goal is to foster #strong[shared understanding] across disciplines, enabling teams to collaborate with purpose and precision. The work where I add the most value starts early, while hardware and software decisions still shape each other — if you are building such a platform, I would welcome the conversation about how I could contribute.
